//! {"name": "channel-rotate", "kind": "modifier", "from": "the wave shader's closing blend", "note": "c*.4 + c.brg*.6 + c*c. The swizzle rotation is what gives that shader its iridescence. WARNING, and it is why this is off by default: it SHIFTS HUE, so anywhere hue carries meaning (the state codebook) it destroys the signal. Use on backgrounds, never on a state-bearing object.", "order": 50}
col = col*0.4 + col.brg*0.6 + col*col;
